        "Content": "4 B/R Semi-Detached House in Mature Housing Estate\nThis property is located in a well-maintained housing estate within 1km of Tubbercurry town centre.\n\nBuilt in 2006, this property is timber-framed. While in need of some modest modernisation, the property is spacious, with large living and cooking areas, large bedrooms, and bathrooms. \n\nLarge rear garden offers potential for patio extension, lean-to and other gardening possibilities. Ample side access gives good space from front to back.\n\nLocality\nTubbercurry offers strong local amenities and clubs, including a golf course next door, primary and post-primary schools, GAA and soccer pitches and teams, a running club, drama and musical groups, as well as multiple festivals throughout the year.\n\nThe property is within commuting distance of many of the surrounding large population centres, including Sligo town, Castlebar, and Ballina. It is 10 minutes from the Sligo-Dublin train in Ballymote and 15 minutes from Knock International Airport.\n\nAccommodation\nDownstairs\n\nHall - 5.5 x 1.8m - Laminate floor\nLiving Room - 4.7 x 4m - Open fire, laminate floor, double doors \nDining Room - 3.6 x 3.6m - Laminate floor, patio doors\nKitchen - 2.4 x 2.6m - Laminate floor, built-in units\nW/C - 1.7 x 1.3m - Tiled flooring\n\nUpstairs\n\nLanding - 3.2 x 2.5m - Large landing, access to attic\nPrimary Bedroom w/ Ensuite - 3.7 x 3m - Timber flooring, built-in wardrobe, shower, toilet, basin, semi-tiled\nBedroom 2 - 2.6 x 3.4m - Timber flooring, built-in wardrobe\nBedroom 3 - 2.6 x 2.6m - Carpet, built-in wardrobes\nBedroom 4 - 2.5 x 2.4m - Timber flooring, built-in wardrobes\nFamily Bathroom - 1.7 x 2.4m - Tiled flooring, bathtub, toilet and basin\nHot Press - 0.7 x 1m - Shelving and hot water cylinder\n\nOutside\n\nCobblelock driveway\nFront, side and rear gardens\n\nFeatures\n\nTimber-framed\nDouble-glazed uPVC windows\nPatio and garden\nPrivate driveway\nLarge communal green area\nOil-fired central heating \nMains water\nMains sewage\n\nDistances\n\n1km from Tubbercurry\n10 minutes to Ballymote Train Station\n20 minutes to Knock Airport\n30 minutes to Sligo town\n40 minutes to Castlebar and Ballina\n\nThis is a must view property with plenty opportunity for development\n\nE: info@reamccarrick.ie\nT: 071 91 85050"
      },
